Diagnosis from the failing traces: (1) literal-value mismatches — quoted strings copied verbatim from the question don't match stored values (`'Bachelors'`, `'Korea '`, cartoon title case), producing empty results that are never checked; (2) semantic slips — `< ANY` rendered as `< MIN`, negation over the wrong predicate, `LEFT JOIN` where gold uses inner join, name-only projection where gold selects whole rows; (3) one degenerate off-topic answer caused by truncation at 800 tokens with no repair path. The harness spends only 1 of its 2 allowed calls and never executes anything, so all of these go undetected.

Candidate s3 adds a verify-and-repair loop: execute the draft, probe actual stored literals for equality/LIKE filters when the result is empty or suspicious, then make one focused repair call with the execution evidence plus a short checklist of the observed error patterns. Token budget raised to 1200 to stop mid-query truncation.

